DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The aassmmcc driver provides support for the Apple System Management Con‐
     troller (SMC), as found in Intel based Apple devices.

     The driver possesses a collection of temperature, fan, light, and accel‐
     eration sensor values which are made available through the sysctl(8) in‐
     terface.

     If available, the keyboard backlight is enabled by the driver and can be
     adjusted using the wsconsctl(8) variable _k_e_y_b_o_a_r_d_._b_a_c_k_l_i_g_h_t.

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     acpi(4), intro(4), sensorsd(8), sysctl(8), wsconsctl(8)

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The aassmmcc driver first appeared in OpenBSD 5.9.

AAUUTTHHOORRSS
     The aassmmcc driver was written by Joerg Jung <_j_u_n_g_@_o_p_e_n_b_s_d_._o_r_g>.

CCAAVVEEAATTSS
     Light sensor values may not be available on older products.

     Acceleration sensors are not available and the associated interrupt han‐
     dling is not implemented.

     Besides the sensors, the huge amount of other functions and information
     available from the SMC is not supported.

